Hydro XCPCIO Plus is based on @hydrooj/scoreboard-xcpcio.
Hydro plugin integration is derived from hydro-dev/Hydro, AGPL-3.0-or-later.
https://github.com/hydro-dev/Hydro/tree/master/packages/scoreboard-xcpcio

The initial Hydro-Contest-Batter repository's (formerly Hydro-Contes-Batter)
Apache-2.0 notice is preserved verbatim in licenses/Repository-initial-Apache-2.0.txt from commit
61ea976cc1bc9a392cce0fc7938804b0ce13d2bd. The imported Hydro plugin integration
continues to use its existing AGPL-3.0-or-later license.

The bundled leaderboard application is XCPCIO 0.98.0, MIT License.
https://github.com/xcpcio/xcpcio
Copyright (c) 2020-PRESENT XCPCIO.
Its upstream license is distributed with the generated public assets.
The generated rank engine delegates its buildRank result to lib/award-policy.mjs
to apply shared per-board medal, podium and first-solve rules. Unofficial teams
retain their starred status and may only be eligible for first-solve awards.
Official ranks and visible first solves are recalculated by this adapter.
The build verifies the pinned entry before applying this extension.

School logos in logos/ retain the source resolution from the Hydro Contest Team School
Logo Registry, https://avatar.hydrooj.com/ (fetched by scripts/fetch-logos.mjs).
WebP source files are preserved byte-for-byte. Other source formats are converted
to lossless WebP with their original dimensions and transparency. Source URLs
and SHA-256 hashes are recorded in logos/index.json.
The logos remain the property of their respective institutions.
For CCS clients, logos/png/ contains derived palette PNG copies, at most 160 px,
generated by scripts/logo-png.mjs. The original WebP files remain unchanged.

